PAGE: /marketplace
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [/] GET  /registry/apis                  — list all APIs (merged on-chain + metadata)
        Query params supported: ?category=  ?active=true
        Returns: apiId, name, provider, priceUsd, category, tags, description, slug

  [/] GET  /registry/categories            — dynamic category list for filter bar
        Returns: string[]

  [ ] GET  /registry/apis?search=          — server-side search by name/description
        Currently search is client-side only (filters already-fetched data).
        For large registries, add ?search= query param to /registry/apis.
        Backend change: filter by name/description ILIKE in metadata getBatch.

  [~] GET  /registry/stats                 — total API count for marketplace header
        Exists but not wired to the marketplace page.
        Frontend could show "X APIs available" in the subtitle.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PAGE: /marketplace/:slug  (API detail)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [/] GET  /registry/slug/:slug            — resolve slug → full API detail
        Returns: apiId, name, provider, pricePerCall, priceUsd, category, tags,
                 longDesc, params, codeExample, responseSchema

  [/] GET  /registry/api/:id               — fallback if no slug (raw apiId in URL)
        Returns same shape as above + activity.recentPayments, activity.totalCalls

  PLAYGROUND TAB — needs these:
  [/] GET  /payment/nonce                  — fresh nonce + deadline before signing
        Returns: { nonce, deadline }

  [/] GET  /payment/balance/:address       — show user's USDC balance before call
        Returns: { usdcBalance }

  [~] GET  /api/v1/call/:apiId             — the actual paid call
        Exists and works. One backend change needed:
        CORS must explicitly allow X-Payment header from browser origin.
        Current: app.use(cors())  — uses defaults, may block custom headers.
        Fix: app.use(cors({ allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'X-Payment'] }))

  [/] POST /payment/verify                 — optional pre-flight check before call
        Returns: { valid, reason }

  RECENT CALLS TAB:
  [/] GET  /registry/api/:id               — activity.recentPayments already returned
        Frontend just needs to wire the tab to display activity.recentPayments
        instead of the hardcoded empty state.

